---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="TPM — A Technical Product Manager in your terminal">
  <section style="padding: 3rem 0 2rem;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 2.8rem; line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 1rem;">
      A Technical Product Manager, in your terminal.
    </h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: #4d4d4d; max-width: 40rem;">
      TPM audits your software product the way a senior PM would. It reconstructs what you intended,
      walks the product as real users, computes the delta, and specs the highest-leverage fixes —
      deterministic, auditable, fast.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <a href="/upgrade" class="button">Get started — $20/month</a>
      <a href="/docs" class="button secondary" style="margin-left: 0.5rem;">Read the method</a>
    </p>
    <pre style="margin-top: 2rem; max-width: 40rem;"><code>npm install -g tpm
tpm init
tpm audit https://yoursaas.com</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section style="padding: 2rem 0; border-top: 1px solid #e4e4e0;">
    <h2 style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">The method is the product.</h2>
    <p style="max-width: 40rem;">
      Every TPM audit runs the same six-stage pipeline. Each stage produces a validated YAML artifact.
      The method is fixed; only the inputs change.
    </p>
    <ol style="max-width: 40rem; margin-top: 1rem;">
      <li><strong>Intent extraction</strong> — Lean Canvas reconstructed from code + marketing surfaces.</li>
      <li><strong>Observed critical path</strong> — Playwright walks the product as each persona.</li>
      <li><strong>Delta analysis</strong> — classifies every step and names the intent mismatches.</li>
      <li><strong>Leverage prioritization</strong> — ranks problems with an explicit argument, not a formula.</li>
      <li><strong>Solution specs + prototypes</strong> — the top 5 fixes, each with a working HTML prototype.</li>
      <li><strong>Artifact assembly</strong> — spec.md + spec.pdf, PM-grade.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section style="padding: 2rem 0; border-top: 1px solid #e4e4e0;">
    <h2>Built for product owners who know what they're looking at.</h2>
    <p style="max-width: 40rem;">
      TPM won't tell you to add confetti animations or rainbow gradients. It finds the step in your signup that
      every honest user abandons, the page where your marketing copy contradicts the product, and the feature
      whose code exists but no user can reach it. Then it gives you a structured fix with a prototype.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
